# sm111, the north-road doubter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm111
revision 3
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent light broad
tier full
written_for cty_willa_wheatcombe
written_by claude
title the north-road doubter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk distrusts_anything_from_the_city
likes mutton_stew singing quiet_chapel frosty_mornings
dislikes bad_manners drizzle
fears letting_the_old_ones_down city_folk_buying_up_the_fields
hopes a_strip_of_ground_in_my_own_name a_winter_of_hard_frost_and_no_drizzle
topics work +0.4 land +0.3 season +0.3 faith +0.2 memories +0.2 food +0.2 gossip -0.3 travel -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the fields out of the granary: quiet, tired and restless, slow to trust anything that came down the north road, singing low in the rows, and feeling the old ones of the family watching every cut.

words
oath! = By the whetstone and the stook | Stubble and frost
saying! = Nothing from up north comes without a hook in it | The furrow knows who cut it | A row's only straight when you look back at it
sickle = the old sickle | the sickle with the worn grip
whetstone = the whetstone | the grey whetstone in my pocket
northroad = the north road | the road up to the city
citymade = city-made | stamped up north
cityfolk = city folk | the ones from up north
stew = mutton stew | a pot of mutton and barley
frostmorn = a frosty morning | white frost on the stubble
drizzle = this drizzle | thin wet drizzle
rows = the rows | the long rows
stooks = the stooks | the sheaves stood up in the stubble
oldones = the old ones | my gran and hers before her
fieldsong = a field song | an old song for the rows
quietchapel = the empty chapel | the chapel with nobody in it
nomanners = no manners | manners like a goat at a gate
granary = the granary | the granary door
weary = bone-weary | worn to the stalk
strip = a strip of my own | a bit of ground with my name on it
lane = the lane | our lane
well = the well | the village well
owls = the barn owls | the owls
seed = seed corn | the seed
tune = a tune | an old tune
feast = the feast | the harvest feast
learner = a learner | a youngster to teach

any
opinion @1 city against 3 : Everything that comes down #northroad# wants something back. I've not met the exception yet. | Cloth, seed or promises, if it's #citymade# I'll pass it by.
opinion @2 city against 3 [world.times=hard|lean] : Lean weeks here, and still #cityfolk# want their share of our grain. #oath#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A loaf costs what it costs and my #wages# don't stir. Somebody's doing well out of that, and it's not me.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses own a fair part of what I've ever cut, and not one of them has stood in #rows# to look at it.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each season's a notch tighter than the last. Up north they've never had to loosen a belt.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A road's honest enough. It's what comes down it I keep an eye on, #address#.
opinion @1 church for 1 : Give me #quietchapel# on a weekday. The Bright One hears me better without a crowd in the way.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I'll stand at the back of #feast#, so long as somebody starts #tune#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new face is welcome once it's done a season in the fields. Not before, #address#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger#'s only a #stranger#. Tell me which road they walked in on and I'll tell you more.
opinion @1 drink mixed 1 : One cup of #ale# at the harvest supper. Two, and I start singing, and then nobody gets home.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Mind the stubble; it's sharp underfoot. | #greet#. You'll be wanting something, I expect.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=farmer] : #greet#. Talk while I cut, if you like. | #greet#. I'm at #rows# till the light goes.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. First light's the best of the day. | #greet#. Early for you, and late for me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be out on #lane#. | #greet#. The day's done, near enough.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn here.season=winter here.weather=clear] : #greet#. #frostmorn.capitalize#, and I'm glad of every bit of it.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Get off your feet before you drop. | You'll want feeding. There's #stew# on.
line @1 again.open : You again. #welcome_back#. | Twice in one day, #address#. I'll start keeping count.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Well enough, thank you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I'd hoped it was you. | #greet#. Sit a minute, then.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I can't stop long. | #greet#. Walk with me down the row.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. It's late for visiting. | #greet#. Quick, then; I'm for #bed#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep to the field path.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #s8_night#. | #farewell#. Keep your lantern low.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #s8_byeback#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #s8_nightback#. | #farewell#. Sleep sound.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. I'll think on that. | #ack#. Well. That's something to chew.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. First I've heard of it. | #oath#. Nobody brought that to the rows.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | I had that already, #hearsay#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who said so? If it came down #northroad#, I'll wait a while. | #doubt#. Let somebody I know say it here, and then I'll think on it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | That's #bad#. The Bright One keep them all.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. | #good.capitalize#. I'll sing for that one.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. | #tired.capitalize#. Always. Well, though. | #weary.capitalize#, but upright.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. The rows don't get any shorter. | #work.capitalize# never ends, and I've two paws for it.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? | How's your own row going, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. | That's a weight. Sit with it a while.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. | It passes. Most things pass by the next sowing.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. I've #rows# to finish before the light goes. | Not this time. I'm #weary# and there's an early start.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Fair. Another day, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's kind. I'll not forget it, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was nothing. Leave it there.
line @1 congratulate : #congrats#. | #good.capitalize#. That's well earned.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #excuse#. | I'd best get back to #rows#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | That'll do me for talk today.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #s8_okay#.
line @1 ack : #ack#. | #bc_it_is#
line @1 tease.return : Say what you like. I've heard worse in #rows#. | #cheek#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: buy your seed off a neighbour, never off a cart from the north. | Keep #whetstone# in your pocket and the edge looks after itself.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : There's trouble on the roads, they say. Go in company, #address#. | #warn#. And keep off #northroad# after dark.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. Spare me a minute, if you can. | #address.capitalize#. Over here.
rule @whet
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Edge is going. Where's #whetstone#? | Three strokes a side. That's what #gran# always said.

rule @drizzle
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #drizzle.capitalize#. Neither wet nor dry. #annoyed#. | Make your mind up, sky. #grumble#.

rule @frost
when concept=bark here.time=dawn here.season=winter here.weather=clear self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Hear it crunch. #tasty.capitalize#, that. | #frostmorn.capitalize#. That's worth getting up for.

rule @song
when concept=bark working=yes self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Down the row and back again, and the sun on the barley. | #resume#. The verse about the ewe.

rule @supper
when concept=bark here.time=dusk working=no
does aside
cooldown 1d
say #stew.capitalize#, then bed, then the rows again. | Home. #supper.capitalize#. Sleep. In that order.

rule @manners
when concept=bark here.crowd=busy|crowd self.dislikes=bad_manners
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Push past me again and see what happens, #fool#. | #nomanners.capitalize#. Not a word of leave.

scene frost_stubble
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #frostmorn.capitalize#. Best hour of the whole year, this. | Hear the ground crack under you? I'd get up for that alone. | Everything white and still, and nobody up but me and the crows.
b : It's bitter, though. | I hear it. | And me, now.
a : Bitter's honest. It's the wet I can't abide, #oath#. | Few stop to listen. Most folk hurry over it to get #snug#. | And you. Stand a minute; it'll be gone once the sun's up, #address#.

scene drizzle_day
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #drizzle.capitalize# again. It wets you through and does the fields no good at all. | I'd take a downpour over #drizzle#. At least a downpour means it. | My fur's damp from the inside out. #annoyed#.
b : The ground wants water, though. | A downpour's no better. | Dry off by a fire, then.
a : The ground wants proper #rain#. This is spit, #address#. | It is. It comes, it's done, and the ditches fill. | I will. Then back out to get #very# wet again.

scene dry_sky
when topic=weather|land here.weather=clear here.season=summer here.region=southmeadow
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Not a cloud again. It's #hot# in the rows by mid-morning. | I keep looking south for #rain# like it owes me money. | #well.capitalize#'s lower than it was. I put a stick down it to see.
b : It'll break soon. | Does it ever pay up? | How much lower?
a : Maybe. I'll not hold my breath for it. | Late and short. Same as my #wages#. | A finger. I'll try again tomorrow, and it'll be two. #grumble#.

scene city_seed
when topic=work|land self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A cart came round selling #seed# from the city. I sent it on its way. | They want us sowing #citymade# barley now. Bigger heads, they say. | Somebody asked what I thought of the new #seed#. I told them straight.
b : What was wrong with it? | Bigger heads? | What did you say?
a : Nothing I could see. That's what worried me, #address#. | Bigger heads on weaker stalks. One good #wind# and it's flat. | That my #gran#'s seed grew in this dirt, and the city's never has.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | That'd be a waste. | Fair enough.

scene city_stamp
when topic=smalltalk|prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I turn a thing over before I buy it. If it says #citymade#, back on the stall it goes. | Bought a pail at market. Turned it over and it was #citymade#. Took it back. | Folk laugh at me for it. Let them. Nothing made down #lane# has ever cheated me.
b : That's a lot of turning over. | What was wrong with the pail? | Nothing at all?
a : A lot less work than being #cheated#. | It'd have rusted by spring. They always do, #oath#. | Not once. I can't say the same for #cityfolk#.

scene north_road_news
when topic=gossip|news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody at #well# had news from the city. I let it go past me. | I don't trust a tale that's walked down #northroad#. It picks things up on the way. | Half what's said in the rows came from up north, and half of that's #nonsense#.
b : Didn't you want to hear it? | Picks up what? | And the other half?
a : I heard it. I'm only not keeping it. #bc_i_know# | Bits that weren't in it when it set out. #bc_they_always_do# | The other half's ours. That I'll listen to, #address#.

scene carts_in
when topic=caravan|harvest world.wagons=in
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The carts are in. Full ones going back up #northroad#, I'll be bound. | Carts in the yard, and every one of them will leave heavier than it came. | I count what the carts take away from #granary#, not what they bring.
b : That's trade, isn't it? | Isn't that how it works? | What do they take?
a : Trade for them. We get the sacks back empty, #address#. | It's how it works for #cityfolk#. | Our grain, mostly. And our best months with it. #grumble#.

scene mutton_stew
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Give me #stew# after a day in the rows. That's food that knows what work is. | There's a pot on at #home# since dawn. Mutton, barley, a turnip if I'm lucky. | #cityfolk.capitalize# put herbs in their stew. Little green bits. I pick them out.
b : Sounds filling. | Lucky with a turnip? | Herbs are nice.
a : It holds you till noon the next day. #bc_it_does# | Turnips cost #money#, these days. Some weeks it's mutton and hope. | Nice for them. A stew should taste of the sheep, #address#.

scene field_song
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I sing at #work#. Low, so nobody hears. Keeps my paws in time. | There's #fieldsong# my #gran# sang, and hers before. I've kept every verse. | I don't talk much. I'll sing, though, given a reason and #tune# worth it.
b : What do you sing? | How many verses? | What's a good reason?
a : Old ones. The kind that go at the pace of #sickle#. | Fourteen. Eleven of them are about the same ewe, #address#. | A harvest in, a wedding, a pot of #stew#. Any of those.
b : #bc_lovely# | Ha. | #bc_fair_enough#

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #quietchapel#. A weekday, the sun on the wall, nobody talking. | I go in when there's no service. The Bright One and I get on better without a sermon between us. | I sing in #quietchapel# sometimes. It carries, in there.
b[job=priest] #priest : The doors are open on service days too. | None taken. The Bright One hears both ways. | I'll leave the door shut for you.
b : It's peaceful then. | Better without? | I'd like to hear that.
a@priest : I know. I come when I can stand a crowd, #address#. | #good.capitalize#. Then we understand each other. | #thanks#. I'll sing the louder for it.
a : Peaceful's the word. Nobody asks you anything. #bc_it_is# | No offence to the priest. I only say more when it's #little# quieter. | You won't. I stop the moment the door opens.

scene faith_old_ones
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say a word for #oldones# every Restday. Somebody ought to. | Prayers aren't much in my line. A dry harvest gets a thank-you from me, and that's my lot. | The Dark One sends the blight, my #gran# said. The Bright One sends the frost to kill it.
b : Do you think they hear? | Is that enough? | Is that true?
a : I think it does me #good# to say it. That'll do. | It's honest. I'd sooner short and meant, #address#. | True or not, I'm glad of the frost. #bc_every_year#

scene gran_sickle
when topic=work|memories self.job=farmer self.age>=25
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : #sickle.capitalize# was my #gran#'s. The grip's worn to the shape of another paw. | My #mum# cut these same rows, and hers before that. Some mornings I feel them watching. | I was sharpening a blade before I could write my name. I still can't write it #very# well.
b : That's a lot to carry. | Watching? | Blade first, letters after.
a : It's light enough. It's the keeping of #oldones#' ways that's heavy. | Not unkindly. Counting how straight I cut, that's all, #address#. | That's the right order, out here. #bc_it_is#

scene old_ones_watching
when topic=dreams|family self.job=farmer
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some nights I dream #oldones# walk the rows behind me, checking my work. | I'd like to do one thing #oldones# never did. Just the one. | Some days I think of leaving the trade. Then I hear my #gran# and pick the sickle up.
b : Do they find fault? | What thing? | What does your #gran# say?
a : Never aloud. That's worse, #address#. | Hold #strip#. Not the farm's, not the House's. Mine. | Nothing. Only looks at me. Worse than any words, #oath#.

scene with_spouse
when topic=family|home self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : With #self.spouse#, I don't need to talk. That's the best of it, #address#. | My #self.spouse_word# is the one I'd trust with my #gran#'s sickle. | I'd not have wed anybody from up north. I wanted one I could understand, #address#.
b : That's a good sort of quiet. | That's trust. | That's sensible.
a : The best sort. Words cost, after a #tired# day. | It is. I don't hand it out, #address#. | Sensible or stubborn. Both, likely. #bc_probably#

scene restless_plan
when topic=dreams|work
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've a jar at #home#. A penny a week goes in it. | #someday.capitalize# I'll have #strip#, and grow what I like on it. | I can't sit still on Restday. I end up weeding somebody else's beans.
b : For what? | What would you grow? | Whose beans?
a : #strip.capitalize#. It'll take a lifetime at this rate. | Barley, same as now. Only mine, #address#. | Anybody's. Nobody's complained yet. #bc_ha#
b : Worth it, though. | #bc_fair_enough# | Ha.

scene tired_bones
when topic=health
does tell.self / sympathise / assess
a : My back's one long ache, shoulders to tail. #bc_every_day# | I'm #weary#. Every night. And every morning I get up anyway. | Cut my paw on a thistle stalk. It's mending, but #slow#.
b : #sympathy#. | That's hard work for you. | Keep it clean.
a : Kind of you. A night's sleep and #stew#, and I'll do. | It is. Nobody ever said #work# would be easy. | I wash it every night. It stings worse than the cut did, #oath#.

scene bad_manners
when topic=smalltalk|day self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A wolf pushed past me at #well# today. Not a word. #nomanners.capitalize#. | You can tell #cityfolk# by their elbows. Never a by-your-leave. | I'll forgive nearly anything but a wolf who won't return a greeting.
b : Some folk are like that. | Not all of them. | That's fair.
a : They are. I don't have to like it, #address#. | Not all. The ones I've met, though. #bc_mostly# | It costs no #money# to answer. None at all.

scene hard_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / assess
a : Lean weeks. I've had #stew# without the mutton twice now. | Everyone's tightening, and #cityfolk# don't feel it. | I count every penny twice. They don't stretch any further for it. #grumble#.
b : Hard all round. | Do they know, up there? | Nobody's do.
a : Hard here. I'd like to see it hard somewhere else for once, #address#. | They know. Knowing costs them nothing. #bc_they_always_do# | No. Except up #northroad#, where there's plenty.

scene good_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Times are #good#, so folk tell me. My #wages# haven't heard yet. | Coin's about. I bought new boots. Made down #lane#, mind. | Everyone's cheerful. I keep waiting for the catch.
b : Maybe this time. | Down the lane? | Maybe there isn't one.
a : Maybe. I'll keep my purse shut till I'm sure. #bc_we_will_see# | Never a #citymade# boot on my feet. #oath#. | There's always one. It's not come down #northroad# yet.

scene harvest_rows
when topic=harvest|work here.season=autumn self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #work.capitalize#. Up before light, home after dark, and singing in between. | #stooks.capitalize#. Straight as a ruler, every row of them. | We're behind on the top field. I'll be out there by lantern if I must.
b : You must be worn out. | Straight rows, then. | By lantern?
a : #weary.capitalize#. Happy, though, in a #tired# sort of way. | Straighter than last year. #oldones.capitalize# would nod at that. | It's been done before. My #gran# did it most harvests.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_good# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene spring_sowing
when topic=season|work here.season=spring self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sowing. I walk the field with the bag and count my steps, #address#. | Spring's for sowing, and for hoping #seed#'s honest. | The furrows are in. Now we wait, and watch the sky.
b : Count them? | Honest seed? | And then?
a : Fourteen to the row, and a handful every fourth. My #gran# taught me that. | Seed from down #lane#. I know where it's been. | Then it comes up or it doesn't, and we start again. #saying.capitalize#.

scene owls_dusk
when topic=animals here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #owls.capitalize# are out over the fields. I stop and watch them every time. | An owl came down so close tonight I felt the air move. #surprise#. | I like #owls#. They work the fields by night the way we do by day.
b : They're good for mice. | Didn't it scare you? | Never thought of it that way.
a : Better than any cat, and quieter, #address#. | No. It scared the mouse. #bc_ha# | Nobody does. They only see a bird.

scene teaching
when topic=work self.master=yes self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm meant to take on #learner#. I'd want one who doesn't chatter. | The trick isn't the cutting. It's knowing when to stop. That takes years to teach. | Anyone can swing #sickle#. Swinging it all day without hurting yourself, that's the trade.
b : Most learners chatter. | When to stop? | How long to learn that?
a : I know. I'll teach the quiet ones first. #bc_i_will# | When the stalk's ripe, and not a day before. You feel it in the paw. | A season to learn it, and the rest of your life to stop forgetting it, #address#.

scene gossip_death
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=death
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll say a word for #topic.them# in #quietchapel#. | Heard it in the rows: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #pity#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, they're saying. I keep thinking of the ones left.
b : I'm sorry to hear it. | That's very hard. | It's a sad thing.
a : So am I. It sits heavy, #address#. | It is. I'll not say more; it's not mine to tell. | It is. I'll sing for #topic.them#, quiet, when I'm alone.

scene gossip_crime
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=theft|violence|wanted
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Word is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm keeping my door barred. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd want it from the watch before I believed it. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, so they say. That's #bad# news for the lane.
b : Sensible. | So would I. | It is.
a : Barred and bolted. I sleep the better for it. | Gossip's cheap. Proof costs more, #address#. | Bad enough. I'll keep #sickle# by the door a while.

scene gossip_glad
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=marriage|newcomer|promise_kept
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I hear #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #good.capitalize#. I'll sing at that. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Nice to hear something kind, for once. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's news I don't mind passing on.
b : That's lovely. | It is, for once. | Nor would I.
a : It is. I've #tune# for it already. | Makes a change from the price of bread, #address#. | There's little enough of it. Pass it on, #address#.

scene newcomer_where
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New faces in #lane#. I'd like to know where from before I say good day. | There's talk of somebody new. I'll make up my own mind. | A newcomer's welcome in the fields. They can show what they're worth there.
b : Does it matter where? | You'll meet them soon enough. | That's fair.
a : To me it does. If they came down #northroad#, I'll watch them. | I will. And I'll take my time over it, #address#. | Slow and fair. That's how it's done here, #address#.

scene feast_songs
when topic=festival self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There'll be singing at #feast#. I'll go for that, and not much else. | I like #feast# from the back of the room, where the songs are loudest. | Everyone's dancing. I'd rather sing. Leave me a bench and #tune#.
b : You don't dance? | The back's the best spot? | I'll leave you one.
a : Not if I can help it. Two left feet and both #weary#. | It is. You see everyone and nobody sees you, #address#. | #good.capitalize#. I'll sing the second verse for you.

scene our_speech
when topic=accent self.away=no
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cityfolk.capitalize# say we sound like a barn door. I'd rather a barn door than a city mouth. | We wish each other #greet# here and mean it. Up north they say good day and don't. | I talk the way my #gran# talked. I'll not trade it.
b : It's a good way to talk. | Do they not mean it? | Nor should you.
a : #thanks#. It's served us this long. | Not that I've ever noticed, #address#. | I won't. Not for any #money#.

scene field_lore
when topic=lore here.region=southmeadow
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : The chapel gets our opening sheaf every harvest. I've carried it twice, #address#. | They say the fields here once ran to the edge of the sky, and nobody owned a furrow. | My #gran# said the old wolves buried a sickle under the mill for luck. Nobody's dug to check.
b : Twice? That's an honour. | Nobody? | Best not to.
a : It's heavy, is what it is. The honour's lighter. #bc_it_is# | Nobody. Then the Houses came with their ledgers. #grumble#. | Best not. Luck's luck. #bc_it_is#

scene stay_put
when topic=travel
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Past the toll gate's #far# enough north for me. | Folk come back from the city talking different. I don't want to talk different. | A walk to the next farm is travel enough for me, #address#.
b : Not even once? | Different how? | It's a long walk, mind.
a : Once would be once too many. #bc_never# | Quicker. As if they've somewhere better to be. | Long enough to be glad I'm #home#. #oath#.

scene first_light
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Up before the cockerel. Always am. | First light's the only quiet I get all day, #address#. | First light, and the dew still on #rows#. That's my hour.
b : Early riser. | Quiet's precious. | It's a good hour.
a : Since I could walk. #oldones.capitalize# were the same. | It is. Then the day starts talking. #bc_every_day# | The best. Nobody's asked me for a thing yet.

scene friend_trust
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend#'s the one I'd want beside me in #rows#. | I don't keep many friends. #self.friend# is enough, #address#. | I'd trust #self.friend# with my #gran#'s sickle. That's as high as I go.
b : That's a good friend. | One good one's plenty. | That's high.
a : The best. I'd not say it out loud, mind. | It is. I'd not swap for ten. #bc_never# | It is. Nobody else gets near it.

story gran_whetstone [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : My #gran# gave me a whetstone the day I first cut a whole row without stopping.
  : Said it had kept three sickles sharp and would see out mine too.
  : I've worn a dip in it since. It's kept #sickle# keen ever since.
  ask : Have you anything handed down like that?
  b[old] : A few things. Fewer every year.
  b : Not a thing, sadly. You keep that one safe.

story rain_charm [topic=lore|memories self.age>=30]
  : Back when I was a #child#, a peddler came down #northroad# selling rain charms. Little tin suns on a string.
  : My #mum# bought one and hung it on the door. Not a drop all summer.
  : #mum.capitalize# kept it, after. Said it showed what the city's promises were worth.
  b : Ha. Did it ever rain?
  : The next spring. The charm took the credit, of course. #bc_ha#

story first_frost [topic=season|memories self.likes=frosty_mornings]
  : #frostmorn.capitalize#, the first I remember. I ran out and wrote my name in the white on the gate.
  : By the time I fetched my #mum# to see, the sun had taken all but the first letter.
  ask : What's the first weather you can remember?
  b : Rain, I think. Rain on a roof.
  b[old] : Snow higher than a door. Or I dreamt it.

story chapel_heard [topic=faith|pastimes self.likes=singing]
  : I was singing in #quietchapel# once, thinking I was alone.
  : When I finished, somebody at the back said "again". I never saw who, #oath#.
  : So I sang it again. Then I went out the side door, #very# quick.
  b : Ha. Maybe it was the Bright One listening.
  b[job=priest] : It might have been me. I'll never tell.

story first_harvest [topic=work|harvest self.job=farmer self.age>=25]
  : My first harvest, I cut faster than anyone in #rows#, to show them.
  : By the third day my paws were raw and I could barely hold #sickle#.
  : My #gran# said nothing. Only handed me a pot of grease and set a slower pace beside me.
  ask : Did anybody ever teach you a thing without a word?
  b : Plenty. The quiet ones teach best.
  b[old] : Every lesson I kept, I learned that way.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#. Speak up; I've #rows# waiting.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You're back. | #topic.player#. #greet#. What's wanted this time?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. Be quick, and I'll be civil, #address#.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : What do you want? Forgive me if I don't smile, #stranger#.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Cutting, binding, sowing, the lot, same as #oldones#. | Out past #granary# by dawn, home by dark. The rows don't care how #tired# you are.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# | Whatever the day wants. I don't make it ask twice, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. #hearsay.capitalize#, mind.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# in #lane#. I keep my head down.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing I'd trust. What there is came down #northroad#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry tales. #work.capitalize# is load enough.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Folk say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I'll pass on, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. The fields don't hurry, and nor do I. #bc_it_is#
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the stubble on your way.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : You want to learn the fields? #learn_offer# Ask, then. | It's not a trade you learn by talking. Still. #go_ahead#.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : I've #learner# already. Ask what you like, though.
dlg @1 master.work : Up before light, a blade in your paw, and no stopping till the row's done. #bc_every_day# | Sowing, weeding, cutting, binding. Whatever the season wants, it wants now, #address#.
dlg @1 master.wages : No #wages# for learning. You work beside me, learn it quicker than alone, and what you make is yours to sell.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : One learner at a time, and one I trust. You'll do. Ask me straight, #address#.
dlg @2 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : One learner at a time, and one I trust. #here.take_on_why#
dlg @1 master.taken : #learn_taken# And no chatter in the rows.
dlg @1 master.refused : #topic.why# | Not yet, #address#. #topic.why#
dlg @1 master.bye : #farewell#. First light, if you want to watch.
graft resident.hub
choice Why don't you trust the city? -> city
node city
say Everything that comes down #northroad# wants something back. Seed, cloth, coin, news. I turn it over and look for the hook.
mood calm
free
choice Is there always a hook? -> hook
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hook
say Not always. But my #gran# was never cheated by a thing made in #lane#, and nor have I been. I'll keep to that.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice Is that an old sickle? [self.job=farmer] -> sickle
node sickle
say Older than me. My #gran#'s, and my great-gran's before. The grip's worn to another paw, and I've grown into it.
mood warm
choice Would you teach me with it? -> sickle_teach
choice Back to the trade. -> learn
node sickle_teach
say You'll learn on your own. This one stays with me. When you've earned #sickle# worth keeping, you'll know.
choice Fair. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
